mode: "100644"
text: "# The CUTS framework — direct a 4K, multi-shot, motion-driven clip\n\nKling isn't the all-round or the control tool — it's the **4K + multi-shot + motion-transfer**\nproducer. Reach for it for native 4K/60fps, a multi-shot sequence in one clip, its unique Motion\nControl, or strong image-to-video at low cost. For production dialogue → **veo-3**; for edit-control/\nconsistency → `runway`. CUTS keeps a human directing — with consent and\ndisclosure as the spine.\n\n## C — Compose the shots (the AI Director)\n- Use **Multi-Shot** to storyboard up to **6 connected cuts** inside one ~15s clip — give each a shot\n  size, camera, and beat; Kling holds spatial continuity.\n- Introduce **characters/props up front** and keep descriptions consistent so they don't drift.\n- Plan for ~15s total; for longer, stitch in the edit (extension drifts after ~30–60s).\n\n## U — Use motion (Kling's edge)\n- Describe **dynamic motion** concretely (\"camera tracks back as the subject strides forward\").\n- **Motion Control:** transfer a motion pattern from a **reference video** onto your subject (clean\n  solo motion transfers best; crowded reference degrades). **Consented/owned reference only.**\n- For in-frame text (brand/price/headline), state it explicitly — Kling renders text well.\n\n## T — Tie identity with references\n- **Image-to-video is Kling's strongest mode** — animate a clean product/character still.\n- Lock identity with **reference images (~4)** or a **3–8s reference video**; use Elements (up to 9\n  images / 3 videos / 3 audio) for multimodal control.\n\n## S — Scale resolution & ship\n- Render **native 4K/60fps** when the job needs it; otherwise 1080p to save credits.\n- **Audio is a guide track** (~3/5) → add final dialogue via **ai-voiceover**, captions via\n  **captions-and-clipping**. Keep crowds ≤5; **verify** physics/hands; **Draft Mode** to iterate cheap.\n\n## The spine: consent + disclosure (never optional)\n- **Motion Control / Avatar only on consented performers / your own / licensed talent.** Never\n  transfer a real, non-consenting person's motion, face, or performance (deepfake).\n- **Disclose** AI-generated video (EU AI Act; TikTok auto; YouTube Altered-Content).\n\n## The shot brief a request should fill\n```\nSHOTS: 1–6 cuts; per cut: shot size + camera + beat (multi-shot, ~15s total)\nMOTION: described motion; Motion Control reference (consented)?\nIDENTITY: image-to-video still? reference images/video to lock character/product\nSCALE: 4K vs 1080p; aspect; Draft Mode to test\nFINISH: audio = guide track -> ai-voiceover; captions -> captions-and-clipping\nCONSENT + DISCLOSURE: confirmed\n```\n"
